"""
ROM data for enemy randomization (EnemyRando.py): 
spawn tables used by AP, every enemy spawn point, each stage's vanilla preload rows, 
the disk-drop table, and one row per enemy type (species).
"""

# Information regarding each enemy type (species). Contains the following in order:
# Enemy id
# Its static motion, aka animation frames, (None if it has no sheet of its own, which means it is only spawned alongside another enemy), 
# Whether it takes damage ('yes' / 'NO' / '?'), 
# The enemy ids its own code adds, 
# The other sheets it draws with (Generator Cannon's Keatons are SM114), 
# How many metatiles above its spawn tile its sprite reaches in any frame, 
# Whether killing it can count for a disk (its death runs TryDropZakoDisk), 
# The most hit points for the enemy, highest if it has multiple segments, can be none which represents unknown, 
# How many metatiles across its widest frame is.
